WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.883
Little John and Will Scarlet were sitting outside the Blue Boar Inn.

2
00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:10.411
A young man arrived on a beautiful white horse.

3
00:00:10.412 --> 00:00:16.910
The man was dressed in silk and velvet clothing, which was trimmed with gold and jewels.

4
00:00:16.911 --> 00:00:19.464
He hurried toward Little John and Will.

5
00:00:19.465 --> 00:00:23.640
"Do you know where I can find Robin Hood?" he asked.

6
00:00:23.641 --> 00:00:26.232
"What do you want with him?" Will demanded.

7
00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:30.317
He was suspicious of any stranger asking about Robin.

8
00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:34.090
"I have a message from Queen Eleanor," the young man said.

9
00:00:34.091 --> 00:00:36.915
"It's important. I'm her page."

10
00:00:36.916 --> 00:00:41.612
Will and Little John looked at each other, unsure of what to do.

11
00:00:41.613 --> 00:00:46.326
Little John shrugged. "This page seems harmless," he said.

12
00:00:46.327 --> 00:00:49.116
"I think we can take him to Robin."

13
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:55.414
Will nodded, and soon the two men were guiding the page through Sherwood Forest.

14
00:00:55.415 --> 00:00:59.070
Robin was sitting under a tree with several of his men.

15
00:00:59.071 --> 00:01:02.353
Alan of Dale was playing his harp and singing.

16
00:01:02.354 --> 00:01:05.761
Robin got to his feet when he saw the men coming.

17
00:01:05.762 --> 00:01:11.152
He was surprised to see the finely dressed page deep in the woods.

18
00:01:11.153 --> 00:01:15.978
"Tell me, what brings you to Sherwood Forest?" asked Robin.

19
00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:20.337
The page climbed down from his horse and bowed to Robin.

20
00:01:20.338 --> 00:01:23.633
"I bring greetings from Queen Eleanor," he said.

21
00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:29.156
"King Henry is holding a very large shooting match in London in four days.

22
00:01:29.157 --> 00:01:32.579
All the best archers in England will be there.

23
00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.971
Queen Eleanor would like you and some of your men to compete."

24
00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:41.108
"I'm honored." Robin bowed his head.

25
00:01:41.109 --> 00:01:45.820
"The queen promises to protect you and send you safely home."

26
00:01:45.821 --> 00:01:48.579
The page held out a gold ring.

27
00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:52.308
"She gives you this ring as a sign of her promise."

28
00:01:52.309 --> 00:01:55.216
Robin placed the ring on his little finger.

29
00:01:55.217 --> 00:02:04.776
"Get ready, Will and Little John! We're going to London!"

30
00:02:04.777 --> 00:02:10.039
After several days of travel, the three men arrived at the palace.

31
00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.990
Queen Eleanor looked happy to see them.

32
00:02:12.991 --> 00:02:17.245
She greeted them with a smile and made sure they had plenty to eat.

33
00:02:17.246 --> 00:02:21.576
"I've heard so much about you," she said.

34
00:02:21.577 --> 00:02:27.288
"But I'd like to hear more. Tell me about your adventures."

35
00:02:27.289 --> 00:02:30.643
So Robin and his men told her many tales.

36
00:02:30.644 --> 00:02:35.622
She especially liked the story about the Bishop of Hereford and the feast.

37
00:02:35.623 --> 00:02:42.138
"We made him stay with us in Sherwood Forest for three days!" said Little John.

38
00:02:42.139 --> 00:02:44.212
The queen laughed at that.

39
00:02:44.213 --> 00:02:49.427
"I hope you're as good at archery as you are at telling stories!"

40
00:02:49.428 --> 00:02:53.581
She lowered her voice and explained her plan.

41
00:02:53.582 --> 00:02:56.497
The next morning was bright and sunny.

42
00:02:56.498 --> 00:03:01.150
Hundreds of archers gathered on a large field, ready to compete.

43
00:03:01.151 --> 00:03:06.482
King Henry and Queen Eleanor sat on thrones trimmed in silver and gold.

44
00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:10.984
A trumpet sounded, and the archers lined up in neat rows.

45
00:03:10.985 --> 00:03:15.908
Robin, Little John, and Will Scarlet hid themselves among the people watching.

46
00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:22.719
Instead of their usual green clothes, the three men wore blue to disguise themselves.

47
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.973
"Queen Eleanor will tell us when it's time to appear," said Robin.

48
00:03:26.974 --> 00:03:30.058
"For now let's enjoy the shooting match."

49
00:03:30.059 --> 00:03:34.513
In the first round, each archer shot seven arrows.

50
00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:37.176
"Wow!" exclaimed Will.

51
00:03:37.177 --> 00:03:41.053
"This is the biggest shooting match I've ever been to!"

52
00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:45.142
It took a long time to get through that first round.

53
00:03:45.143 --> 00:03:48.003
And then there were several more rounds.

54
00:03:48.004 --> 00:03:52.350
As the day wore on, more archers were eliminated.

55
00:03:52.351 --> 00:03:56.140
At last only three men remained.

56
00:03:56.141 --> 00:03:58.727
Queen Eleanor turned to King Henry.

57
00:03:58.728 --> 00:04:03.330
"Do you think those are the best archers in England?"

58
00:04:03.331 --> 00:04:06.339
The king gazed at the archers proudly.

59
00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:11.363
"Those men are from my guard," said the king.

60
00:04:11.364 --> 00:04:14.953
"They're the best in the world!"

61
00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:21.074
"Well, I know three men who are better archers," said the queen.

62
00:04:21.075 --> 00:04:26.866
The king laughed. "What do you know about archery?"

63
00:04:26.867 --> 00:04:32.663
The queen smiled. "You might be surprised by my knowledge.

64
00:04:32.664 --> 00:04:38.474
The three men will enter the contest, but you must promise not to harm them.

65
00:04:38.475 --> 00:04:45.299
After the contest you must allow them to travel freely for forty days."

66
00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:53.118
King Henry looked puzzled. "Those are strange conditions, but I promise."

67
00:04:53.119 --> 00:04:56.039
The queen motioned for her page.

68
00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:03.838
She whispered in his ear, "Tell Robin and his men it's time for their match."

69
00:05:03.839 --> 00:05:07.186
"My dear," said the king.

70
00:05:07.187 --> 00:05:11.436
"You have such an interest in archery now.

71
00:05:11.437 --> 00:05:14.356
Shall we bet on this match?

72
00:05:14.357 --> 00:05:19.469
I'll bet two hundred fine bows and arrows."

73
00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:25.175
"I'll bet this beautiful belt." The queen pointed to her waist.

74
00:05:25.176 --> 00:05:30.129
"Its jewels are worth far more than your bows and arrows."

75
00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:34.552
People began whispering, wondering what the queen was up to.

76
00:05:34.553 --> 00:05:41.210
One thing was certain: this promised to be an interesting match!

